 sets of x-values. The bars have a width of 0.8 (a standard for the graphin=
g library <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://matplotlib.org/" class=3D"g-=
md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">Matplotlib</a>, a=
nd we want the bars to be touching. We would want the first blue bar to be =
at x =3D 0.0, and the first orange bar to be at x=3D0.8, so that the bars a=
re touching.  The second blue bar would go at x=3D2.0, and the second orang=
e bar at x=3D2.8, and so on.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Instead of calculating each one of these by hand, we ca=
